  "HDDS-9668": {
    "jira_id": "HDDS-9668",
    "issue_type": "Improvement",
    "resolution": "Implemented",
    "title": "Zero-Copy in EC GRPC (write)",
    "description": "Today EC with GRPC copies input data buffer several times:\r\n * when parsing protobuf objects from the input network stream, data is copied from the original netty direct buffer to heap.\r\n * when writing data to files, the heap buffer needs to be copied to direct buffers by NIO.\r\n\r\nThe cost of buffer copies themself is inefficient, it comes with GC consequences of cleaning up the intermediate buffers. Those together slow EC I/O down.\r\n\r\n!ec-ncopies.png|width=807,height=292!\r\n\r\nWe can use the ZeroCopyMarshaller from RATIS-1932 to avoid all those issues.",
    "commits": [
      {
        "sha": "fd2732bb92abab8917bb860298ebf01cd0fb2006",
